From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sf2000-linux <sf2000-linux@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 19:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: speed up diagnostic pulses

The retained RAM progress log now gives exact boot positions after a watchdog
reset. Keep the backlight and status LED pulses, but shorten them so physical
test iterations spend less time replaying stages that are already recorded in
log.txt.
---
 arch/mips/kernel/setup.c | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c b/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c
index 1bdd89323..2a3e5c928 100644
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c
@@ -85,11 +85,11 @@
 #define SF2000_PIN_R05 5
 #define SF2000_STATUS_L25 (1u << SF2000_PIN_L25)
 #define SF2000_BACKLIGHT_R05 (1u << SF2000_PIN_R05)
-#define SF2000_STAGE_OFF_TICKS 0x00020000u
-#define SF2000_STAGE_ON_TICKS 0x00010000u
-#define SF2000_STAGE_GAP_TICKS 0x00040000u
-#define SF2000_TICK_OFF_TICKS 0x00010000u
-#define SF2000_TICK_GAP_TICKS 0x00020000u
+#define SF2000_STAGE_OFF_TICKS 0x00008000u
+#define SF2000_STAGE_ON_TICKS 0x00004000u
+#define SF2000_STAGE_GAP_TICKS 0x00010000u
+#define SF2000_TICK_OFF_TICKS 0x00004000u
+#define SF2000_TICK_GAP_TICKS 0x00008000u
 #define SF2000_QEMU_DIRECT_DELAY_SHIFT 12
 #define SF2000_GMA_KSEG1 ((volatile unsigned char *)CKSEG1ADDR(0x18808000))
 #define SF2000_GMA_DESC_KSEG1 ((volatile unsigned int *)CKSEG1ADDR(0x00f00000))
-- 
2.50.1
